window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-7969ca0198aaf47f"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"developer-settings\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">开发者设置</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取文档页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>本页按使用入口分节介绍设置：ChatGPT 网页版、桌面应用、Codex CLI 和 IDE（集成开发环境）扩展。先确认你正在使用哪一种入口，再查看对应部分。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 网页版会在 ChatGPT 设置中保存产品和工作区偏好。ChatGPT Work 对话运行在受管理的环境中，不会读取本地 Codex 配置文件。请使用工作区在 ChatGPT 设置中提供的控件；部分设置可能由工作区管理员代为管理。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>通用<a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257\">设置</a>页面介绍应用偏好设置，包括个人资料、键盘快捷键、通知、外观、个性化、记忆和已归档的对话。</p> <p><a id=\"project-and-terminal-behavior\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">项目与终端行为</h2> <p>选择文件的打开位置、对话中显示多少命令输出，以及终端标签页默认打开的位置。</p> <p><a id=\"code-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">代码审查</h2> <p>在<strong>设置 &gt; Git</strong>中，使用<strong>审查交付方式</strong>选择<strong>内嵌</strong>，以便在可能时于当前对话中运行 <code>/review</code>；也可以选择<strong>独立对话</strong>，另行启动审查对话。</p> <p><a id=\"ide-extension-sync\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"ide\">IDE 扩展同步</h2> <p>当 ChatGPT 桌面应用和 IDE 扩展打开同一个项目时，两者会共享当前对话和编辑器上下文。在应用的提示输入框中开启 <strong>IDE 上下文</strong>，Codex 就可以使用编辑器当前打开的文件。若希望应用提示词不包含编辑器上下文，请关闭此选项。</p> <p>你可以从 IDE 扩展打开应用对话，也可以在应用中继续 IDE 对话。两种界面会使用同一个项目来确定要共享哪些对话和上下文。</p> <p><a id=\"agent-configuration\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">智能体配置</h2> <p>应用中的 Codex 智能体与 IDE 扩展和 CLI 共用相同配置。常用设置可通过应用内控件调整；高级选项可编辑 <code>config.toml</code>。详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">智能体审批与安全</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>。</p> <h2 id=\"git\">Git</h2> <p>使用 Git 设置统一分支命名方式，并选择 Codex 是否可以强制推送。你还可以设置提示词，让 Codex 据此生成提交消息和拉取请求说明。</p> <p><a id=\"integrations-and-mcp\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"mcp\">集成与 MCP</h2> <p>通过模型上下文协议（MCP）连接外部工具。你可以启用推荐服务器，也可以添加自己的服务器。如果服务器需要 OAuth，应用会启动身份验证流程。由于 MCP 配置保存在 <code>config.toml</code> 中，这些设置也适用于 Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展。详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">模型上下文协议</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"browser-developer-mode\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">浏览器开发者模式</h2> <p>在<strong>开发者模式</strong>下，开启<strong>启用完整 CDP 访问权限</strong>，即可允许 ChatGPT 使用 Chrome DevTools Protocol 进行性能分析和更深入的浏览器调试。如果你的组织已禁用完整 CDP 访问权限，你就无法在本机启用它。设置方法、风险、审批和管理员要求请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809?sectionMissing=app-developer-mode\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">开发者模式（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex CLI 从 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 读取个人默认设置。如果需要针对特定项目覆盖设置，请在受信任的项目或子文件夹中添加 <code>.codex/config.toml</code> 文件。CLI 和 IDE 扩展共用这些配置层。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-your-settings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">查看设置</h2> <p>使用以下命令查看当前会话实际生效的设置：</p> <ul> <li>运行 <code>/status</code>，查看当前模型、审批策略、可写入根目录和 Token（词元）用量。</li> <li>运行 <code>/debug-config</code>，查看按优先级排列的配置层，以及受管理策略要求的来源。</li> <li>使用 <code>--strict-config</code> 启动 Codex，将无法识别的 <code>config.toml</code> 键视为错误，而不是忽略它们。</li> </ul> <p>完整的交互式命令参考请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">开发者命令</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"change-settings-for-one-run\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">为单次运行更改设置</h2> <p>如果有专用标志，请优先使用。常见示例包括 <code>--model</code>、<code>--sandbox</code>、<code>--ask-for-approval</code>、<code>--profile</code> 和 <code>--search</code>。使用 <code>-c</code> 或 <code>--config</code> 可在单次运行中覆盖任何受支持的配置键。</p> <p>下面的模型覆盖示例需要有权使用 GPT-6.1 Sol。如果你的账户或工作区无法使用该模型，请省略 <code>--model</code>，或选择 <code>/model</code> 列出的模型。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">各套餐中的 GPT-6.1 Sol 可用情况</a>。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex --model gpt-6.1-sol\ncodex --profile deep-review\ncodex --config model_reasoning_effort='\"medium\"'\n</code></pre> <p>命令行标志和 <code>--config</code> 值具有最高优先级。完整标志列表请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">开发者命令</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"configuration-layers\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">配置层</h2> <p>CLI 会先应用命令行标志和 <code>--config</code> 覆盖项，然后依次处理项目、配置档案、用户、系统和内置设置。你可以利用此优先级，将共享默认值保存在配置文件中，并通过命令行进行一次性更改。</p> <p>完整优先级顺序和常用选项请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"change-settings-in-the-tui\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"tui\">在终端界面（TUI）中更改设置</h2> <p>TUI 是在终端窗口中以文本方式交互的界面。Codex 的交互式终端界面提供了用于更改常用会话和显示设置的选择器：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>目标</th> <th>命令</th> <th>相关配置</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>选择终端模式</td> <td><code>/tui</code></td> <td><code>tui.fullscreen_transcript</code>（需要重启）</td> </tr> <tr> <td>选择模型</td> <td><code>/model</code></td> <td><code>model</code>, <code>model_reasoning_effort</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>更改权限</td> <td><code>/permissions</code></td> <td>审批和沙箱设置</td> </tr> <tr> <td>配置可选工具</td> <td><code>/experimental</code>, <code>/memories</code></td> <td>特定功能的 <code>config.toml</code> 键</td> </tr> <tr> <td>自定义终端界面</td> <td><code>/keymap</code>, <code>/statusline</code>, <code>/title</code>, <code>/theme</code></td> <td><code>[tui]</code> 下的键</td> </tr> <tr> <td>设置编辑默认项</td> <td><code>/vim</code>, <code>/raw</code></td> <td><code>tui.vim_mode_default</code>, <code>tui.raw_output_mode</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>某些命令只对当前会话生效，另一些选择器则会询问是否保存选择。若要将设置作为未来会话的默认值，请设置对应的配置键。有关终端主题、编辑器、补全和快捷键工作流，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-2a01a9d34cde2424\">CLI 自定义</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"settings-references\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">设置参考</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">高级配置</a>介绍配置档案、一次性覆盖和其他高级工作流。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>列出可用的键和值。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f52101a0e13391a3\">配置示例</a>提供完整的示例文件。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-22d54b5578c4f826\">环境变量</a>介绍 CLI 和安装程序使用的变量。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex IDE 扩展有两个设置层：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Codex 设置</strong>控制与 Codex CLI 共用的智能体行为，包括模型、推理强度、权限、沙箱、MCP 服务器和个性化设置。Codex 从 <code>config.toml</code> 读取这些设置。</li> <li><strong>编辑器设置</strong>控制扩展在 VS Code 及兼容编辑器中的行为。这些设置使用编辑器设置系统中的 <code>chatgpt.*</code> 键。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"open-codex-settings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">打开 Codex 设置</h2> <p>选择 Codex 侧边栏中的齿轮图标，然后选择 <strong>Codex 设置</strong>。常用智能体控件可在设置面板中调整；也可以选择 <strong>打开 config.toml</strong>，直接编辑当前生效的配置层。</p> <p>配置层顺序和常用键请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>。所有受支持的 <code>config.toml</code> 键请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"change-an-editor-setting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">更改编辑器设置</h2> <p>若要更改设置，请按以下步骤操作：</p> <ol> <li>打开编辑器设置。</li> <li>搜索 <code>@ext:openai.chatgpt</code>、<code>Codex</code> 或设置名称。</li> <li>更新对应的值。</li> </ol> <p>Codex 对话界面也会遵循 VS Code 内置的聊天字体设置。</p> <p><a id=\"editor-settings-reference\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">编辑器设置参考</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>设置</th> <th>默认值</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.commentCodeLensEnabled</code></td> <td><code>true</code></td> <td>在 <code>TODO</code> 注释上方显示 CodeLens，便于 Codex 处理这些注释。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.openOnStartup</code></td> <td><code>false</code></td> <td>扩展启动完成后聚焦到 Codex 侧边栏。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.followUpQueueMode</code></td> <td><code>queue</code></td> <td>选择运行期间发送的消息是等待下一次运行（<code>queue</code>），还是引导当前运行（<code>steer</code>）。扩展会将旧版 <code>interrupt</code> 值视为 <code>steer</code>。按 <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> 可为单条消息反转此行为。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.composerEnterBehavior</code></td> <td><code>enter</code></td> <td>选择按 <kbd>Enter</kbd> 是否始终发送（<code>enter</code>）；按 <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> 是否发送多行提示词（<code>cmdIfMultiline</code>）；或者是否始终要求使用修饰键（<code>cmdAlways</code>）。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.reviewDelivery</code></td> <td><code>inline</code></td> <td>尽可能在当前对话中运行 <code>/review</code>（<code>inline</code>），或启动单独的审查对话（<code>detached</code>）。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.localeOverride</code></td> <td>Auto（自动）</td> <td>设置 Codex 界面的首选语言。留空时会自动检测。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.runCodexInWindowsSubsystemForLinux</code></td> <td><code>false</code></td> <td>仅限 Windows：当 WSL 可用时，在 WSL 中运行 Codex。如果代码库和工具位于 WSL2，或需要 Linux 原生工具，可启用此项。更改后会重新加载 VS Code。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.cliExecutable</code></td> <td>Unset（未设置）</td> <td>仅用于开发：设置 Codex CLI 可执行文件的路径。除非你正在开发 Codex CLI，否则不需要设置此项；手动覆盖捆绑的可执行文件可能导致扩展的部分功能无法使用。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chat.fontSize</code></td> <td>Editor default（编辑器默认值）</td> <td>控制 Codex 侧边栏中的聊天文字，包括对话内容和提示输入框。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chat.editor.fontSize</code></td> <td>Editor default（编辑器默认值）</td> <td>控制 Codex 对话中以代码形式呈现的内容，包括代码片段和差异。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>以上 <code>chatgpt.*</code> 键属于 IDE 扩展，不应写入 <code>config.toml</code>。有关共用的智能体设置，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>、<a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">高级配置</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"developer-settings\">Developer settings</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT web stores product and workspace preferences in ChatGPT settings. ChatGPT Work chats run in a managed environment and don't read local Codex configuration files. Use the controls your workspace exposes in ChatGPT settings; workspace administrators may manage some settings for you.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The general <a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257\">Settings</a> page covers app preferences, including profile, keyboard shortcuts, notifications, appearance, personalization, memories, and archived chats.</p> <h2 id=\"project-and-terminal-behavior\">Project and terminal behavior</h2> <p>Choose where files open, how much command output appears in chats, and where terminal tabs open by default.</p> <h2 id=\"code-review\">Code review</h2> <p>Under <strong>Settings &gt; Git</strong>, use <strong>Review delivery</strong> to choose <strong>Inline</strong> to run <code>/review</code> in the current chat when possible or <strong>Detached</strong> to start a separate review chat.</p> <h2 id=\"ide-extension-sync\">IDE extension sync</h2> <p>When the ChatGPT desktop app and IDE extension are open in the same project, they share active chats and editor context. Turn on <strong>IDE context</strong> from the app composer to let Codex use files currently open in your editor. Turn it off when you want the app prompt to exclude that editor context.</p> <p>You can open an app chat from the IDE extension and continue an IDE chat in the app. Both surfaces use the same project to determine which chats and context to share.</p> <h2 id=\"agent-configuration\">Agent configuration</h2> <p>Codex agents in the app inherit the same configuration as the IDE extension and CLI. Use the in-app controls for common settings, or edit <code>config.toml</code> for advanced options. See <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Agent approvals and security</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a> for details.</p> <h2 id=\"git\">Git</h2> <p>Use Git settings to standardize branch naming and choose whether Codex uses force pushes. You can also set prompts that Codex uses to generate commit messages and pull request descriptions.</p> <h2 id=\"integrations-and-mcp\">Integrations and MCP</h2> <p>Connect external tools through Model Context Protocol (MCP). Enable recommended servers or add your own. If a server requires OAuth, the app starts the authentication flow. These settings also apply to the Codex CLI and IDE extension because MCP configuration lives in <code>config.toml</code>. See <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Model Context Protocol</a> for details.</p> <h2 id=\"browser-developer-mode\">Browser developer mode</h2> <p>Under <strong>Developer mode</strong>, turn on <strong>Enable full CDP access</strong> to let ChatGPT use the Chrome DevTools Protocol for performance profiling and deeper browser debugging. If your organization has disabled full CDP access, you can't enable it locally. See <a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809?sectionMissing=app-developer-mode\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Developer mode (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> for setup, risk, approval, and administrator requirements.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex CLI reads your personal defaults from <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>. Add a <code>.codex/config.toml</code> file to a trusted project or subfolder when you need project-specific overrides. The CLI and IDE extension share these configuration layers.</p> <h2 id=\"inspect-your-settings\">Inspect your settings</h2> <p>Use these commands to understand the effective settings for the current session:</p> <ul> <li>Run <code>/status</code> to see the active model, approval policy, writable roots, and token usage.</li> <li>Run <code>/debug-config</code> to see the configuration layers in precedence order and the source of managed policy requirements.</li> <li>Start Codex with <code>--strict-config</code> to treat unrecognized <code>config.toml</code> keys as errors instead of ignoring them.</li> </ul> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Developer commands</a> for the full interactive command reference.</p> <h2 id=\"change-settings-for-one-run\">Change settings for one run</h2> <p>Use a dedicated flag when one exists. Common examples include <code>--model</code>, <code>--sandbox</code>, <code>--ask-for-approval</code>, <code>--profile</code>, and <code>--search</code>. Use <code>-c</code> or <code>--config</code> to override any supported configuration key for one run.</p> <p>The model override below requires GPT-6.1 Sol access. If it isn't available to your account or workspace, omit <code>--model</code> or choose a model listed by <code>/model</code>. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol availability by plan</a>.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex --model gpt-6.1-sol\ncodex --profile deep-review\ncodex --config model_reasoning_effort='\"medium\"'\n</code></pre> <p>Command-line flags and <code>--config</code> values have the highest precedence. For the complete flag list, see <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Developer commands</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"configuration-layers\">Configuration layers</h2> <p>The CLI applies command-line flags and <code>--config</code> overrides before project, profile, user, system, and built-in settings. Use that precedence to keep shared defaults in configuration files and one-off changes on the command line.</p> <p>For the complete order and common options, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"change-settings-in-the-tui\">Change settings in the TUI</h2> <p>The interactive terminal UI provides pickers for common session and display settings:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Goal</th> <th>Command</th> <th>Related configuration</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Choose a terminal mode</td> <td><code>/tui</code></td> <td><code>tui.fullscreen_transcript</code> (restart required)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Choose a model</td> <td><code>/model</code></td> <td><code>model</code>, <code>model_reasoning_effort</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Change permissions</td> <td><code>/permissions</code></td> <td>Approval and sandbox settings</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Configure optional tools</td> <td><code>/experimental</code>, <code>/memories</code></td> <td>Feature-specific <code>config.toml</code> keys</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Customize the terminal UI</td> <td><code>/keymap</code>, <code>/statusline</code>, <code>/title</code>, <code>/theme</code></td> <td>Keys under <code>[tui]</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Set editing defaults</td> <td><code>/vim</code>, <code>/raw</code></td> <td><code>tui.vim_mode_default</code>, <code>tui.raw_output_mode</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Some commands apply only to the current session, while some pickers offer to save the choice. Set the related configuration key when you want a default for future sessions. For the terminal theme, editor, completions, and shortcut workflows, see <a href=\"#/article/a-2a01a9d34cde2424\">CLI customization</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"settings-references\">Settings references</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">Advanced configuration</a> covers profiles, one-off overrides, and other advanced workflows.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration reference</a> lists the available keys and values.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f52101a0e13391a3\">Sample configuration</a> provides a complete example file.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-22d54b5578c4f826\">Environment variables</a> documents variables used by the CLI and installer.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The Codex IDE extension has two settings layers:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Codex settings</strong> control agent behavior shared with Codex CLI, including the model, reasoning effort, permissions, sandbox, MCP servers, and personalization. Codex reads these settings from <code>config.toml</code>.</li> <li><strong>Editor settings</strong> control how the extension behaves inside VS Code and compatible editors. These settings use <code>chatgpt.*</code> keys in the editor's settings system.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"open-codex-settings\">Open Codex settings</h2> <p>Select the gear icon in the Codex sidebar, then select <strong>Codex Settings</strong>. Use the settings panel for common agent controls, or select <strong>Open config.toml</strong> to edit the active configuration layer directly.</p> <p>For the configuration layer order and common keys, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a>. For every supported <code>config.toml</code> key, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration reference</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"change-an-editor-setting\">Change an editor setting</h2> <p>To change a setting, follow these steps:</p> <ol> <li>Open your editor settings.</li> <li>Search for <code>@ext:openai.chatgpt</code>, <code>Codex</code>, or the setting name.</li> <li>Update the value.</li> </ol> <p>The extension also honors VS Code's built-in chat font settings for Codex chat surfaces.</p> <h2 id=\"editor-settings-reference\">Editor settings reference</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Setting</th> <th>Default</th> <th>Description</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.commentCodeLensEnabled</code></td> <td><code>true</code></td> <td>Show CodeLens above <code>TODO</code> comments so Codex can address them.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.openOnStartup</code></td> <td><code>false</code></td> <td>Focus the Codex sidebar when the extension finishes starting.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.followUpQueueMode</code></td> <td><code>queue</code></td> <td>Choose whether messages sent during a run wait for the next run (<code>queue</code>) or steer the current run (<code>steer</code>). The extension treats the legacy <code>interrupt</code> value as <code>steer</code>. Press <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> to invert the behavior for one message.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.composerEnterBehavior</code></td> <td><code>enter</code></td> <td>Choose whether <kbd>Enter</kbd> always sends (<code>enter</code>), <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> sends multiline prompts (<code>cmdIfMultiline</code>), or the modifier is always required (<code>cmdAlways</code>).</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.reviewDelivery</code></td> <td><code>inline</code></td> <td>Run <code>/review</code> in the current chat when possible (<code>inline</code>) or start a separate review chat (<code>detached</code>).</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.localeOverride</code></td> <td>Auto</td> <td>Set the preferred language for the Codex UI. Leave empty to detect it automatically.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.runCodexInWindowsSubsystemForLinux</code></td> <td><code>false</code></td> <td>Windows only: Run Codex in WSL when WSL is available. Use this when your repositories and tooling live in WSL2 or when you need Linux-native tooling. Changing this setting reloads VS Code.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.cliExecutable</code></td> <td>Unset</td> <td>Development only: Set the path to the Codex CLI executable. You don't need this setting unless you're developing the Codex CLI; manually overriding the bundled executable can prevent parts of the extension from working.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chat.fontSize</code></td> <td>Editor default</td> <td>Control chat text in the Codex sidebar, including chat content and the composer.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chat.editor.fontSize</code></td> <td>Editor default</td> <td>Control code-rendered content in Codex chats, including code snippets and diffs.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>The <code>chatgpt.*</code> keys above belong to the IDE extension and don't go in <code>config.toml</code>. For shared agent settings, use <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a>, <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">Advanced configuration</a>, and the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration reference</a>.</p>"};
